<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding a limit of a definite integral</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Given that \(\displaystyle \int_{1}^{k} \left({@pp*x+qq@}\right)dx = {@V@}\), where \(k > 1\):</p><p>(a) find the integral in terms of \(k\);</p><div>\(\displaystyle \int_{1}^{k} \left({@pp*x+qq@}\right)dx =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) find the value of \(k\).</p><div>\(k =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Integrate, substitute the limits \(k\) and \(1\), and subtract; then set the result equal to {@V@} and solve the quadratic.</p><p>(a) \[\int_{1}^{k} \left({@pp*x+qq@}\right)dx = \left[{@pp/2*x^2+qq*x@}\right]_1^k = \left({@Fk@}\right) - {@F1@} = {@ta1@}\]</p><p>(b) \({@ta1@} = {@V@}\), so \({@pp/2*k^2+qq*k-F1-V@} = 0\), which factorises as \({@pp/2*(k-kk)*(k-k2)@} = 0\). So \(k = {@kk@}\) or \(k = {@k2@}\). The upper limit must be greater than \(1\), so \(k = {@kk@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_k(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [k])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Your answer should be an expression in k only.";
/* Design: find an unknown limit. [pp, qq, kk, k2, V]; k is the learner's symbol, never a variable. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 11, Exercise C question 4. */
L: [[2,2,3,-5,12],[2,3,4,-7,24],[2,4,4,-8,27],[2,5,4,-9,30],[6,6,4,-6,63],[6,12,3,-7,48],[6,18,3,-9,60],[8,8,3,-5,48],[8,16,3,-7,64],[8,24,3,-9,80]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
pp: L[ix][1]; qq: L[ix][2]; kk: L[ix][3]; k2: L[ix][4]; V: L[ix][5];
ta1: pp/2*k^2+qq*k-pp/2-qq;
F1: pp/2+qq;
/* diagnostics */
Fk: pp/2*k^2+qq*k;
rv: pp/2+qq-pp/2*k^2-qq*k;
/* 2 d.p. root of the wrong equation pp/2 k^2 + qq k = V (forgot F(1)) */
rw: (-qq+sqrt(qq^2+2*pp*V))/pp;
kwr: float(floor(100*rw+1/2)/100);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
