  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Integration: finding a limit of a definite integral</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.2: Express a definite integral with an unknown upper limit in terms of k, and solve for k.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Exercise C, Question 4 in Chapter 11 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new integrands and values, with a quadratic whose second root is rejected.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
